Set up instructions for the Paragon version;
NOTE: DOS version is also available. The DOS (CLI) version allows multinode/
      multiplayer action! Suggested if your BBS can run this version.

unarc to any directory... Example: Doors:DeepSpace
Don't use spaces in the names of the directories... 'Doors:Deep Space'
Only one player should be allowed to play at once!

**********************************************************************
This part is optional...........

Edit file Text/AlienRaces
You can have the aliens named whatever you wish.
Names have to be 15 characters or less..
The GameSetupP program will create the Aliens from this text file.
2 aliens of each name will be created if there are 25 names or less..
So if you have 25 names you will get 50 Aliens.. 15 you will get 30 ect..
If you have 26 to 50 alien names only 1 Alien will be created for each
name. A possible of 2 to 50 Aliens can be created for the game.

**********************************************************************

Edit file Text/Sysop.txt

Make sure your handle/name (what ever will be past to the game by the BBS)
is on one line in this text file.. This will allow you access to the
Sysop editors in the game.  This file can be edited in the game. The
name 'Sysop' is already in the text file. You can add all your 
Co-Sysops names also if you want to. But I wouldn't! The editors
make it to tempting to cheat:)

At the main menu in DeepSpace you can enter the Planet/Port editor by
hitting '!'. Again only names that are in the Text/Sysop.txt file will
gain access.
Also at the main menu hit '@' to enter the Alien/User editor. Also 
defaults for the game can also be edited from here. How many turns
each ship can have, what ship a new player starts with, how much $$,
shields, ect... Oh yah also the remarks.txt file can be edited from
the defaults editor. This contains insults/sayings that a alien/player
will use when he/she is attacked.

Now before you run DeepSpaceP you have to run GameSetupP from the CLI.
Run this program from the same directory DeepSpaceP is located.
It will create the universe, aliens, ports, ect.. After all the files are
created a 'Registration' menu will appear. Even though you may not
be already registered enter the path of the DeepSpace directory where
prompted before hitting ESCAPE. Example: Doors:DeepSpace
This will save the file ENV:DeepSpaceP/config

You are all ready.. Run the door as a Paragon type as per your BBS's 
instructions..

